+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Shipped              |
+
+`ToolRegistry` owns the boundary between what the model sent and what a tool executor sees. A call
+that does not satisfy the tool's declared `inputSchema` is turned back as a tool result the model can
+read and correct, so no executor has to hand-validate its own input and no consumer reimplements the
+check differently, or not at all.
+
+## Contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved definition's `inputSchema` before
+  calling the executor; a rejected call returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` describes the failure,
+  and the executor is never invoked
+  ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property before the executor runs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-input-validation.acceptance.test.ts#L75)).
+- Input reaching an executor has already passed the declared schema: unknown keys pass through
+  unmodified and nothing is injected, defaulted or coerced
+  ([validated by: passes unknown extra properties through to the executor unchanged, exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-input-validation.acceptance.test.ts#L87)).
+- A rejection message names the failing property path and the expected type, and never carries the
+  offending value
+  ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field naming the path and expected type, without the value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-input-validation.acceptance.test.ts#L98)).
+- A value outside a declared `enum` is rejected before the executor runs
+  ([validated by: rejects a value outside a declared enum before the executor runs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-input-validation.acceptance.test.ts#L111)).
+- A static tool's schema is compiled once at `register` time and not again per call, and an
+  uncompilable schema fails at `register` with a message naming the tool
+  ([validated by: throws at register time for an uncompilable schema, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-input-validation.acceptance.test.ts#L122),
+  [validated by: compiles a static schema once, at register, and not again across ten execute calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-input-validation.acceptance.test.ts#L137)).
+- A schema from a function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` is validated against the schema current at
+  each call, not a stale cached one
+  ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema current at each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-input-validation.acceptance.test.ts#L165)).
+- Neither the rejection text nor any log line carries an input value; rejection messages name property
+  paths and constraints only
+  ([validated by: keeps identifying input values out of rejection text and log lines](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-input-validation.acceptance.test.ts#L193)).
+- A rejected tool call reaches the model as a tool result within the existing tool-round budget:
+  `processMessage` resolves rather than rejecting, and the rejection text is visible to the provider
+  on the next round
+  ([validated by: returns a rejected tool call to the model as a tool result within the same conversation](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-input-validation.acceptance.test.ts#L215)).
+- `execute` still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` for an unregistered name
+  ([validated by: still throws Unknown tool for an unregistered name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-input-validation.acceptance.test.ts#L258)).
+
+## Out of scope
+
+Validating tool *output*, hallucination detection, per-tool authorization, and retry, timeout and
+rate limiting around tool execution are separate concerns. The `Unknown tool: <name>` throw stays a
+throw: the same failure class handled the opposite way is an intentional split, tracked on its own
+issue, because changing it affects direct callers.
